----- correctness fix caught on host (latent compile error the deferred gate would hit) -----
  WidgetPreviews.swift previously applied `.environment(\.widgetFamily, .systemMedium)`
  to three plain-view #Previews. `EnvironmentValues.widgetFamily` is GET-ONLY, so the
  key path is a `KeyPath`, not a `WritableKeyPath`, and `.environment(_:_:)` does NOT
  type-check on it. Proven by isolating the expression against the macOS SDK:
    error: cannot convert value of type 'KeyPath<EnvironmentValues, WidgetFamily>'
           to expected argument type 'WritableKeyPath<EnvironmentValues, V>'
  Fix: removed the three invalid modifiers (the only correct minimal change). The
  remaining `.environment(\.colorScheme, .dark)` / `(\.dynamicTypeSize, .accessibility3)`
  are writable and retained, so the dark-mode + Dynamic-Type preview intent is kept.
  Swept the whole app: no other `.environment(\.widgetFamily,...)` usages exist.
  After the fix, swiftlint/swiftformat remain green and the file's only remaining
  diagnostic is the full-Xcode #Preview macro plugin (above).

